From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Subject: thermal: power_allocator: warn about a missing sustainable-power only where it is used
Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

The power_allocator governor warned that sustainable_power would be
estimated on every thermal zone it binds to, including zones with no
throttling trip where the value is never used. Warn only for zones that have
one.

---
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c b/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c
--- a/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/gov_power_allocator.c
@@ -723,10 +723,17 @@ static int power_allocator_bind(struct thermal_zone_device *tz)
 		params->allocated_tzp = true;
 	}
 
-	if (!tz->tzp->sustainable_power)
-		dev_warn(&tz->device, "power_allocator: sustainable_power will be estimated\n");
-	else
+	/*
+	 * The sustainable power only feeds the PID controller, which works towards
+	 * trip_max. A zone with no passive or active trip (a sensor zone with only a
+	 * critical trip) never runs it, so a missing value is not worth a warning there.
+	 */
+	if (!tz->tzp->sustainable_power) {
+		if (params->trip_max)
+			dev_warn(&tz->device, "power_allocator: sustainable_power will be estimated\n");
+	} else {
 		params->sustainable_power = tz->tzp->sustainable_power;
+	}
 
 	if (params->trip_max)
 		estimate_pid_constants(tz, tz->tzp->sustainable_power,
